    "rich_text_intro": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "text_intro": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Peri-peri is the African bird&rsquo;s eye chili, and the Portuguese-Mozambican marinade built around it &mdash; chili, garlic, lemon, vinegar and paprika. On chicken it is an overnight job. On salmon it is ten minutes, because a fatty fillet takes the spice immediately, and any longer and the acid starts firming the surface before the grill ever gets to it.</p><p>Getaway Plate&rsquo;s version is about as short as a recipe gets: thaw, toss, wait ten minutes, grill. The one piece of technique worth reading twice is the pan &mdash; the fish goes onto a sheet that has been preheating on the grate, not onto the bars, which is what keeps the spice crust on the fish instead of in the fire.</p>",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_font": "body",
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        }
      },
