    "at_a_glance": {
      "type": "multicolumn-with-icons",
      "blocks": {
        "g_time": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "time",
            "custom_icon": "",
            "heading": "About 35 minutes",
            "text": "<p>Twenty-five of prep &mdash; and ten of those are the salmon sitting in the marinade doing nothing. Seven to ten minutes on the grill and it is done.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "g_serves": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "users",
            "custom_icon": "",
            "heading": "Serves 2 to 4",
            "text": "<p>Two portions is dinner for two with a side. Four makes it a platter, which is how it is photographed here and how it is best eaten &mdash; sliced, shared, buried under onion and parsley.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "g_marinade": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "heart",
            "custom_icon": "",
            "heading": "Three things in the bowl",
            "text": "<p>Olive oil, peri-peri blend, salt. Everything else &mdash; sliced onion, parsley, lemon, a last drizzle of oil &mdash; happens after the fish is off the heat.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "g_prep": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "custom_icon": "",
            "heading": "Ten minutes, not thirty",
            "text": "<p>The marinade is short on purpose. Peri-peri carries vinegar and lemon, and a long soak starts to cure the outside of the fillet, which costs you the texture the grill is supposed to give it.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        }
      },
