    "game_plan": {
      "type": "timeline",
      "blocks": {
        "s_thaw": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/peri-peri-salmon-thawing-vacuum-sealed.jpg",
            "subheading": "Step 1",
            "heading": "Submerge and defrost",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text": "<p>Leave the portions in their vacuum seal and submerge them in a bowl of chilled water until completely thawed &mdash; 20 to 30 minutes for a 6 to 8 oz portion, and worth changing the water once. Overnight in the refrigerator works too if you have thought ahead. Never on the counter.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "s_bowl": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/peri-peri-salmon-portions-in-bowl.jpg",
            "subheading": "Step 2",
            "heading": "Out of the pack, into a bowl",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text": "<p>Cut the vacuum packaging open, lift the portions out and put them straight into a mixing bowl. Pat them dry first &mdash; not in the original method, but a dry fillet takes the oil and the blend far better than a wet one, and it is five seconds of work.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "s_season": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/peri-peri-salmon-seasoning-blend.jpg",
            "subheading": "Step 3",
            "heading": "Olive oil first, then the peri-peri",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text": "<p>Olive oil over the fish, then the peri-peri blend. Oil first is the whole trick: it gives the spice something to hold onto instead of drifting to the bottom of the bowl. Toss gently until every face is evenly coated.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "s_marinate": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/peri-peri-salmon-marinating.jpg",
            "subheading": "Step 4",
            "heading": "Ten minutes, and no longer",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text": "<p>Leave it to marinate for ten minutes while the grill comes up to temperature. This is long enough for the spice to bloom in the oil and start pulling at the surface of the fish, and short enough that the vinegar and lemon in the blend have not begun to cure it.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "s_grill": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/peri-peri-salmon-sheet-pan-grill.jpg",
            "subheading": "Step 5",
            "heading": "Preheat the sheet pan with the grill",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text": "<p>Grill to medium-high, baking sheet on the grate while it heats. Season the portions with salt, then lay them on the hot sheet &mdash; that is what stops them sticking, and it keeps the oil and spice out of the flame.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "s_char": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/peri-peri-salmon-grilled-charred.jpg",
            "subheading": "Step 6",
            "heading": "Three to four minutes a side, flip once",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text": "<p>Lid down, three to four minutes, and leave it alone. It releases when the crust has set. Flip once, another three to four minutes, then pull it while the centre is still slightly translucent &mdash; it keeps cooking on the way to the table.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "s_serve": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/peri-peri-salmon-plated-parsley-onion.jpg",
            "subheading": "Step 7",
            "heading": "Onion, parsley, lemon, oil",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text": "<p>Onto a serving platter. Sliced onion over the top, a good squeeze of fresh lemon, an extra drizzle of olive oil and a handful of parsley. Serve immediately &mdash; the onion is meant to be sharp and raw against the char, and it softens if it sits.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        }
      },
